WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.040
Summer.

2
00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.930
A green valley, a river,
cows, a dairy-house.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.420
Here, Tess thrives.

4
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.460
Winter.

5
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.920
A bare grey upland, strewn with flints.

6
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.090
A bent figure hacks at roots in the cold.

7
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.320
On the horizon, a chimney.

8
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:23.220
A steam engine has arrived, and its
driver "was in the agricultural world,

9
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.990
but not of it."

10
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.590
One woman, two farms.

11
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.480
So why does place matter so much?

12
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.330
In this mission, you'll
walk Tess's Wessex,

13
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.480
from the Valley of the Great
Dairies to a "starve-acre place".

14
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.450
You'll ask whether Nature
really feels for Tess,

15
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.500
or simply looks the other way.

16
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:48.120
And you'll meet a countryside in crisis,
in the farming depression of about 1873

17
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.110
to 1896.

18
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.570
Your mission: explain why place matters.
